Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Preserve strict self-development evidence for manual releases while cleanly deferring an ineligible automatic release.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Build the all-feature macOS nextest archive once, extract it at the original workspace path, and fan it out to five bounded consumers.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Discover and fail closed on every tracked Bun/npm lock; resolve all five lock audits and remove duplicate install-time advisory noise.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Keep the dependency-free VS Code lint suite separate from the installed package-graph test; ship Playwright in the VSIX and verify browser capture from the extracted artifact.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Isolate Gemini mutable state, limit lifecycle trust to pinned OpenCode, use exact argv for Unix process-tree ownership, and prevent archived manifests/diagnostics from becoming live projects.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Preserve the complete issue, PR, CI, research, tests-first, and upstream-report record.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	## Root causes and reproduction
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	The baseline contained a real Auto Release policy result in the wrong automatic control flow, three macOS jobs redundantly compiling before nextest partitioning, four vulnerable JavaScript surfaces hidden behind non-blocking install summaries, Gemini harness noise, and archived manifests discovered as dependency projects.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	Fresh exact-SHA runs exposed integration boundaries that local state had masked:
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- Playwright server code followed optional removed `chromium-bidi` paths when bundled into the VSIX.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- OpenCode needs its pinned package-owned postinstall to choose the platform binary.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- nextest's default temporary extraction cannot satisfy legacy compile-time Cargo binary paths.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- the source terminology gate scanned immutable raw evidence, and the requirements aggregate was stale.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- the dependency-backed VS Code bundle test had been appended to a source-only suite that intentionally runs without `vscode/node_modules`.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- artifact transfer/extraction consumed part of the ten-minute macOS job envelope before the 480-second test budget began.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	- command-stream 0.15 inserted a shell between Formal AI's exact argv and the Unix process group, exposing a descendant-termination race at the 20 ms timeout boundary.
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	
Lint and Format Check	Run registered gates (stage rust)	Minimal red/green experiments cover each boundary. The canonical index contains the twelve named baseline logs, initial and pushed-candidate workflow logs, run/job/artifact metadata, check annotations, all three PR discussion surfaces, the reconstructed timeline, nine requirements, solution alternatives, and complete finding ledger:
